{
  "schema": "simant-canonical-publication-v1",
  "prior_commit": "4f5a320",
  "scope": "Five whole TUs (root:0250, root:1E57, root:23E6, root:2505, S23:39C7): remove the duplicate extern declaration blocks inserted before the first behaviour-reviewed function. No definition, type, storage or initializer changes.",
  "root_review": {
    "reviewer": "root",
    "note": "The removed lines only repeated declarations that the same file already makes at their original position. MSC 6.00AX code generation depends on the number of identifiers declared earlier in a file; the inserted blocks made nine previously exact functions inexact (PopUpInfoWindow, DrawCurBalloons, DrawSpider, PrevListLine, f_23E6_0392, win_Recalc, f_2505_0831, f_2505_08EA, f_1E57_0F8E). Without them all nine match the original bytes again and each module verifies as a whole. A /W3 compile of every changed TU reports no implicit function declaration (positive control: C4016/C4071 on an undeclared call), so no call changed its prototype view. The behaviour-reviewed definitions in these TUs are token-identical; their static source reviews stand and their differential contracts are rerun on the new objects."
  },
